# GRUB, target efi: the boot loader of the UEFI firmware (x86_64-efi, arm64-efi, arm-efi: --target is
# the machine of the platform), which grub-install --target=<machine>-efi writes into the EFI system
# partition. A package of its own (GRUB-efi_<ver>) with its own status: the default target is the one of
# the BIOS (i386-pc) on x86_64. The programs are the same, only the modules under /usr/lib/grub/<platform>
# differ
PKG_SUFFIX=-efi
CONF_FLAGS+=" --with-platform=efi"
